  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 308 PM EDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nEarly afternoon RAP analysis shows the UP in between deep 992mb low \npressure near Hudson Bay and 1022mb surface high pressure sprawled \nout over the Northern Plains. Though water vapor imagery indicates \nrather dry midlevel air, plenty of low cloud cover remains over the \nUP, aided by an unseasonably cool airmass moving over the lake and \nupsloping into the western and central UP. This helped to kick off \nlight rain showers over the area earlier today, but rain showers and \nsprinkles are tapering off this afternoon. Winds remain elevated \nthis afternoon behind a cold front, with temperatures already \nfalling into the upper 50s over the northern UP and ranging in the \nlower to mid 60s to the south. Temperatures turn much cooler tonight \nthan in previous days, bottoming out in a refreshing 45-55F range \n(coolest in the interior-central) while skies gradually clear out. \nUnder high pressure, Wednesday looks to be an entirely pleasant, if \nunseasonably cool, summer day with highs ranging in the upper 60s \nand lower 70s under sunny skies. NW winds start off breezy, gusting \nto around 20-25mph over the eastern half of the UP, but fall back \nduring the afternoon as our pressure gradient slackens. Expect \nanother pleasantly cool nights as lows range in the mid 50s to mid \n50s. \n\nHowever, as the high pressure flattens and progresses east through \nthe Lower Great Lakes into New England for Thursday into Friday, \nexpect the temperatures to begin climbing back up to above normal \n(think high temperatures in the upper 70s to mid 80s). As this \noccurs, a weak ridge-rider may graze the UP with some rain showers \nand even a rumble of thunder Thursday night into Friday morning. \nBetter troughing arrives Saturday as low pressure moves through \nOntario, eventually dragging a cold front through the UP Saturday \nafternoon and evening. Ahead of this, temperatures climb even \nhigher, possibly reaching the upper 80s in our typically warmer \nsoutherly downsloping areas in the western UP and along Superior. \nBehind this low, upper-level northwest flow looks to keep \ntemperatures somewhat moderated over us into early next week.",
